  "text": "The short - beaked common dolphin ( Delphinus delphis ) is a species of common dolphin .\nIt has a larger range than the long - beaked common dolphin ( D. capensis ) , occurring throughout warm - temperate and tropical oceans , including the Indian Ocean although in smaller quantities than other places they are found .\nThere are more short - beaked common dolphins than any other dolphin species in the warm - temperate portions of the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans .\nIt is also found in the Caribbean and Mediterranean Seas .\nThe short - beaked common dolphin is also abundant in the Black Sea , Gulf of Mexico , and Red Sea .\nThey follow the gulf stream up to Norwegian waters .\nSeldom do any short - beaked dolphin venture near the Arctic .",
